I'm going to say that this is fine. It's obviously an exaggeration, but it's 
exactly what he meant, which is fine.

Regarding the interpretation of an unbound {da}, it means what it has meant, 
and how Lojbanists who do speak and use Lojban regularly use it. Gejyspa and 
myself both use it the same way, so I'm inclined to leave it how it is. With 
the example of {mi viska re danlu .i roda gerku}, there are SO MANY ways to 
refer back to {re danlu} that I don't understand why you -must- use {da} in 
particular. It's not actually meant to do that, at all. We have all of 
KOhA5, all of GOhA, KOhA pretty much in general, and any substitutive 
context-dependant lerfu ( {dy.} for example).

